<LegalLayout
  title="Disclaimer | StackAutopsy Web3 Security Suite"
  description="Disclaimer of the StackAutopsy Web3 Security & Forensics Suite: as-is provision, no advice, non-custodial, specific technical risks."
  heading="Disclaimer"
>
  <h2>1. Provision "as is"</h2>
  <p>
    The StackAutopsy Web3 Security &amp; Forensics Suite (hereinafter the "Suite") by <strong>AndrexTheDev</strong> is provided
    without warranty of any kind. No guarantee is given for completeness, correctness, freedom from errors, currency
    or availability — in particular not for data originating from external blockchain networks, public
    endpoints or raw data pasted by the user. All check results are <strong>diagnostic indicators</strong>
    that always require independent professional verification.
  </p>

  <h2>2. No investment, financial, legal or tax advice</h2>
  <p>
    No output of the Suite — including that of the DAC8-SelfProof, STVA-UpgradeDiff or BitVault-Stress modules —
    constitutes investment, financial, legal or tax advice. For tax assessments (e.g. evidence in the
    context of EU DAC8, the Travel Rule or national tax documentation) please consult a person authorized to
    provide advice whom you trust. A cryptographic proof of control does not replace a tax-law
    case-by-case assessment.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Non-custodial notice</h2>
  <p>
    The Suite <strong>never stores or transmits private keys or seed phrases</strong>. There
    is no operated server that receives user input; processing takes place locally in the browser.
    Every on-chain transaction (e.g. submitting a prepared refund or revoke calldata) takes place
    exclusively under the sole responsibility of the user and via wallets and
    network endpoints chosen by the user.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Specific technical risks</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Block snapshot dependency (STVA-UpgradeDiff):</strong> simulation and comparison results refer
      to the specifically stated block number and block hash. Later state changes (new implementation,
      changed storage) are not captured by them.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Nonce expiry (7702-SlotGuard):</strong> every regular transaction of your account increments the nonce. A
      pre-signed emergency package (panic-revoke authorization) then loses its redeemability and must be
      <strong>regenerated</strong>. An encrypted emergency package is not a backup substitute, but a
      reaction tool.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Legal case-by-case assessment (DAC8-SelfProof):</strong> a signed audit dossier documents
      cryptographic control at a point in time. Tax recognition (self-transfer, acquisition costs,
      holding periods) is a separate legal question.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Endpoint availability:</strong> public read endpoints may be throttled or offline. The
      modules therefore consistently offer offline modes with manual input; result quality then depends on the
      correctness of the pasted raw data.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Fee and market data:</strong> reference rates or fee assumptions (e.g. paymaster spreads,
      dust cliffs) are model calculations and not a trading offer.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. External content and networks</h2>
  <p>
    No liability is accepted for the content and availability of external networks, block explorers, IPFS gateways
    or wallet software. Links are provided for information purposes and create no liability for third-party content.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Applicable law</h2>
  <p>
    The law of the operator's location applies, excluding conflict-of-laws referral rules, to the extent legally
    permissible. Mandatory consumer protection rights remain unaffected.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
